{"name":"Spring Rain","hex":"#a3bd9c","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"spring","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To move or burst forth.","To appear."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An act of springing: a leap, a jump.","The season of the year in temperate regions in which temperatures and daylight hours rise, and plants spring from the ground and into bloom and dormant animals spring to life."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spring"},{"term":"rain","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Condensed water falling from a cloud.","Any matter moving or falling, usually through air, and especially if liquid or otherwise figuratively identifiable with raindrops."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To have rain fall from the sky.","To fall as or like rain."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rain"}],"entries":[{"title":"April shower","blocks":[{"text":"In parts of the Northern Hemisphere, an April shower is rain during the month of April. One of the major causes of the often heavy downpours is the position of the jet stream. In early spring, the jet stream starts to move northwards, allowing large depressions to bring strong winds and rain in from the Atlantic. In one day the weather can change from springtime sunshine to winter sleet and snow. The track of these depressions can often be across Ireland and Scotland bringing bands of rain followed by heavy showers and strong blustery winds. In France, this meteorological phenomenon is known as \"Giboulées de mars\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c2/Snow_shower_on_Dartmoor.jpg/330px-Snow_shower_on_Dartmoor.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/April_shower"},{"title":"Kawai Gyokudō","blocks":[{"text":"Kawai Gyokudō  was the pseudonym of a Japanese painter in the nihonga school, active from Meiji through Shōwa period Japan. His real name was Kawai Yoshisaburō."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bf/Kawai_Gyokud%C5%8D_photographed_by_Shigeru_Tamura.jpg/330px-Kawai_Gyokud%C5%8D_photographed_by_Shigeru_Tamura.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kawai_Gyokud%C5%8D"},{"title":"Spring Rain (The Go-Betweens song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Spring Rain\" is a song by the Australian alternative rock band the Go-Betweens that was released as the lead single from their fourth album Liberty Belle and the Black Diamond Express in 1986. The single was issued by Beggars Banquet in the UK and Truetone in Australia, failing to chart in the UK and reaching number 92 in Australia."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/e/e4/Spring_Rain_single_cover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spring_Rain_(The_Go-Betweens_song)"},{"title":"Rain","blocks":[{"text":"Rain or rainfall is a form of atmospheric precipitation composed of droplets of water aerosols that have condensed from atmospheric water vapor and fall by gravity. Depending on the intensity, rain can be described as a drizzle, a shower, a cloudburst or a downpour. It is also often accompanied by other weather phenomena such as strong wind (rainstorm) and lightning (thunderstorm), and may be mixed with hail/ice pellet, snow (sleet) and sandstorm. Rain is a major component of the water cycle and is responsible for depositing most of the fresh water on Earth. It provides water for hydroelectric power plants, crop irrigation, and suitable conditions for many types of ecosystems."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/65/Hard_rain_on_a_roof.jpg/330px-Hard_rain_on_a_roof.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rain"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9a/Futsuka_Zuki_by_Kawai_Gyokud%C5%8D.jpg/330px-Futsuka_Zuki_by_Kawai_Gyokud%C5%8D.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/9/9a/Futsuka_Zuki_by_Kawai_Gyokud%C5%8D.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9a/Futsuka_Zuki_by_Kawai_Gyokud%C5%8D.jpg/330px-Futsuka_Zuki_by_Kawai_Gyokud%C5%8D.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFutsuka_Zuki_by_Kawai_Gyokud%C5%8D.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/28/Parting_Spring_by_Kawai_Gyokudo_%28National_Museum_of_Modern_Art%2C_Tokyo%29_L.jpg/500px-Parting_Spring_by_Kawai_Gyokudo_%28National_Museum_of_Modern_Art%2C_Tokyo%29_L.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/28/Parting_Spring_by_Kawai_Gyokudo_%28National_Museum_of_Modern_Art%2C_Tokyo%29_L.jpg/960px-Parting_Spring_by_Kawai_Gyokudo_%28National_Museum_of_Modern_Art%2C_Tokyo%29_L.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/28/Parting_Spring_by_Kawai_Gyokudo_%28National_Museum_of_Modern_Art%2C_Tokyo%29_L.jpg/500px-Parting_Spring_by_Kawai_Gyokudo_%28National_Museum_of_Modern_Art%2C_Tokyo%29_L.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AParting_Spring_by_Kawai_Gyokudo_(National_Museum_of_Modern_Art%2C_Tokyo)_L.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1d/Parting_Spring_by_Kawai_Gyokudo_%28National_Museum_of_Modern_Art%2C_Tokyo%29_R.jpg/500px-Parting_Spring_by_Kawai_Gyokudo_%28National_Museum_of_Modern_Art%2C_Tokyo%29_R.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm